# Agent debugging scratch. Playwright/browser-MCP dumps an accessibility tree per
# snapshot and a PNG per screenshot, both into the repo root. They are throwaway
# diagnostics — the 2026-08-03 session alone left 6 YAML trees and 672KB of PNGs.
# Never commit them: this repo is PUBLIC, and a binary in git history cannot be
# removed without a rewrite (already gated behind the credential rotation in
# docs/SECURITY-ROTATION.md). Diagnose in the browser, keep the finding, drop the file.
.playwright-mcp/
/*.png

# Local-only archive — moved to ~/HoundShield-Local-Archive, never pushed again.
# brain/ was a 47MB duplicate of the knowledge base; legacy/ was 43MB of dead
# code with zero imports (already excluded from tsconfig). Neither is the product.
#
# ANCHORED (`/brain/`, not `brain/`) — this cost a red CI on 2026-08-07. An
# unanchored pattern matches a directory of that name at ANY depth, so it was
# also swallowing `compliance-firewall-agent/components/brain/`, a real source
# directory. Nobody noticed because its one existing file was tracked before the
# rule landed and git keeps tracking what it already tracks. The next file added
# there — components/brain/AnswerText.tsx — was silently never committed: the
# local build passed against it on disk, and CI failed with TS2307 on a module
# that simply was not in the repository.
/brain/
compliance-firewall-agent/legacy/

# Pitch decks — founder direction 2026-08-07: keep local, not in the repo yet.
docs/decks/

# Test + audit artifacts generated by the CI gates (coverage thresholds in
# vitest.config.ts, Lighthouse assertions in .lighthouserc.json). Both are
# regenerated on every run and must never be committed. Anchored to the repo
# root would be wrong here — each package produces its own.
coverage/
.lighthouseci/

# Claire worktree fragments — never belong in the repo
.claire/

# ---- NexusSwift ----------------------------------------------------------
nexusswift/**/__pycache__/
nexusswift/*.db
nexusswift/*.db-wal
nexusswift/*.db-shm

# The blanket `tests/` rule above is meant for scratch fixtures, but it
# matches at any depth and would silently drop NexusSwift's entire 80-test
# security harness from every commit. Git cannot re-include a file whose
# parent directory is excluded, so the directory must be un-excluded first
# and the files second - one line alone does nothing.
!nexusswift/tests/
!nexusswift/tests/*.py
